# Chips, tags, badges, and meta pills

Every small "chip" in the app — a rounded/pill-shaped label with its own
background/border holding a short word or two (brand names, `Mention`/`Link`,
`Visible`/`Not visible`, HTTP codes, `Yes`/`No`, `Single`/`Multiple`, severity
and fix-type badges, engine name badges, status tags like `New`/`Fixed`, etc.)
— uses **13px** text, never 12px.

Pill labels in **page heroes and card headers** — topic chips (`Citations`),
status chips (`Opportunity`, `Winning`), and similar meta tags — use **14px**
text (unchanged, still higher than the 13px table/content-chip floor).

## Spec

```
inline-flex items-center
px-2 py-0.5 (dense chip) or px-2.5 py-1 (hero pill)
rounded-full (or rounded/rounded-md for square-cornered tags)
text-[13px] font-medium   ← dense chip / table content chip
text-[14px] font-medium   ← hero meta pill
border …
```

Never `text-[12px]` on a content/status/category chip. This applies to every
dashboard and shared component — `SevBadge`/`FixBadge`/`ImpactBadge`,
`TypeBadge`/`MentionBadge`/`LinkBadge`, `EngineBadge`/`EngineList`,
`BrandPill`/`BrandsCell`, `Badge`, HTTP-code tags, Yes/No/Single/Multiple/DF/NF
table tags, and any other bespoke status/category `<span>` chip.

## Exceptions — stay at 12px (not content chips)

- **Numeric-only counters and avatars**: a fixed-size circle/square holding
  just a number or a 1–2 letter abbreviation (rank badges, engine avatar
  initials, notification counts, the numeric badge nested inside a filter
  chip like `All (12)`). These aren't word-label chips.
- **Metric delta/change pills**: an arrow + percentage indicating a trend
  (e.g. `↑6.8%`, health-score delta). These are metric indicators, not
  content tags.
- `CountCard.jsx`'s own delta pill and `AdvancedFilterTrigger.jsx`'s active-filter
  count badge are explicitly locked at 12px per the `count-card` and
  `advanced-filter` rules — do not change those two specific components.

## Do not

- Do not leave a brand/status/type/severity/HTTP-code/Yes-No chip at 12px.
- Do not bump numeric counters, avatars, or delta/trend pills to 13/14px —
  keep those at 12px so they stay visually distinct from content chips.
